spec ri03-hub-same-source: 2 sessions, 6 permutations
# RI03 (G8). Two transactions each create one edge sharing an endpoint with the
# other's: x->t1 and x->t2 (same source). The adjacency conflict rule (graph/lpg/mvcc_adjversion.go, rmp #2445)
# claims BOTH endpoints of an append, so the second appender is refused while the first
# is open and after it commits. If appends commuted, as an older comment stated, both
# would commit in every order.
# The final dangling probe must count 0 in every permutation: an edge to a dead node
# is never committed (catalogue §9 point 3).

starting permutation: s1e s1c s2e s2c
step s1e: MATCH (x:N {name:'x'}), (t:N {name:'t1'}) CREATE (x)-[:R {id:1}]->(t) RETURN count(*) AS created
created
-------
1      
(1 row)
step s1c: COMMIT
step s2e: MATCH (x:N {name:'x'}), (t:N {name:'t2'}) CREATE (x)-[:R {id:2}]->(t) RETURN count(*) AS created
ERROR: serialization conflict
step s2c: COMMIT
ERROR: cypher: transaction poisoned by a prior failed Exec statement — call Rollback
final final: MATCH (n) RETURN n.name AS name ORDER BY name
name
----
"t1"
"t2"
"x" 
(3 rows)
final edges: MATCH (x)-[r]->(y) RETURN x.name AS src, r.id AS id, y.name AS dst ORDER BY src, id, dst
src|id|dst 
---+--+----
"x"|1 |"t1"
(1 row)
final dangling: <lpg: arcs touching a dead node, at a fresh snapshot>
live_arcs|dangling
---------+--------
1        |0       
(1 row)

